---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Contribute" description="How to contribute code, content, questions, corrections and resources to this open-source GATE platform." canonicalPath="/contribute/">
  <section class="hero"><div class="wrap"><h1>Contribute</h1><p class="lead">Code, content, questions, corrections, translations, resources, testing, accessibility. Every factual claim needs a source; official facts need official sources.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap grid cols-2">
    <div class="card"><h3>Categories</h3><ul><li>Code / design / a11y / tests</li><li>Topic guides (follow the topic template)</li><li>Original practice questions (never copy coaching banks)</li><li>Corrections with sources</li><li>Resources (free, last-checked)</li></ul>
      <div class="btn-row"><a class="btn primary small" href="https://github.com/issues/new?title=%5Bquestion%5D+Proposed+original+question&body=Paper%3A%0ASubject%3A%0ATopic%3A%0AType+%28MCQ%2FMSQ%2FNAT%29%3A%0AQuestion%3A%0AOptions%3A%0AAnswer%3A%0AExplanation%3A%0ASource%3A+original" rel="noopener">Submit a question →</a><a class="btn ghost small" href="https://github.com/issues/new?title=%5Bresource%5D+Suggest+resource&body=Title%3A%0AURL%3A%0ASubject%3A%0AWhy+useful%3A%0ACost%3A" rel="noopener">Suggest a resource →</a></div>
      <p class="meta">Forms open pre-filled GitHub issues — nothing is silently submitted. No fake success messages.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Review pipeline</h3><p><code>Draft → source check → technical review → copyright check → build validation → publish → periodic review</code></p><p>Statuses: <code>draft / review / published / needs-review / archived</code>. AI drafts require human review; official facts are never auto-published.</p><p><a href="/report-error/">Report an error →</a> · <a href="/changelog/">Changelog</a></p>
      <h3>Code of conduct (short)</h3><ul><li>Be kind, cite sources, respect copyright.</li><li>No paid-material uploads, no spam, no rank guarantees.</li><li>Maintainers may edit or decline contributions with reasons.</li></ul>
      <p class="meta">Open source (MIT): inspect, fork, improve. This page documents the process honestly — no backend forms pretending to send.</p></div>
  </div></section>
</Base>
